    "turn_text": "I mean, this is such a, it's such a quandary. It is because When you have somebody who's striking you and harming Americans, you have to hit them and hit them twice as hard. But if this becomes like an actual campaign that takes us into something that would resemble a war, an actual war, you got to go to Congress. You got to ask them, I'm not here to say Joe Biden should not be directing the armed forces to strike back. I want us to strike back. I do. But if it's more than getting the people that just did it, if like immediately you had Lindsey Graham, who's the war hawk and John Cornyn here from Texas talking about go and take out Tehran, go and fight Iran right now. I mean, you can't just say that. And then it happens. There's actually a process of declaring war if you're going to go and do some big war move. And that's my problem. I'm okay with him striking back, but at what point do you say? You got to go talk to Congress about this and get the authority. He doesn't just have the authority to go to war. That would be a dictator. So when I have any big zone, he's going to talk about that because I think it's a very important delineation. Can you just say I'm going to go and do that? And the answer is no, if it's more than just retaliation because you don't want to go through the process. Hey, can I hit back at the bad guys that just hit us? No, go ahead and back. You want to go into some sort of like they're calling it national guard troops and getting ready to send them to the region. You know what I mean, Kerry? That's different.",
